# `M154d` / `C42` — a second `tflw.config`, and it exists because of something the scoping got
# wrong.
#
# The plan assumed `viewport` was a per-env key and budgeted a dedicated `env constructsViewport`
# for it, on the blast-radius precedent of `safetyRedaction` and `logConfig`. It is not: `viewport`
# is legal **only in `defaults`** (`TF025`, "move it to the `defaults` block"), so a project has
# exactly one browser window size and no env can vary it. Writing the env first is how that was
# found — `tflw check` refused it.
#
# That makes a root-level declaration unusable for a plant. `defaults` is project-wide, so
# `viewport 900 600` in the root config would re-lay-out the storefront underneath `C34`'s masked
# snapshot baselines and `C35`'s axe counts — a plant that broke two other plants to grade itself.
#
# tflw reads its config from **`join(cwd, 'tflw.config')`** (`cli.ts:1106`), never by walking up
# from the test file, so a corpus with its own directory has its own defaults and touches nothing
# else. That is the same mechanism `tflw-acceptance/*/` already runs on.
#
# 900x600 is deliberately far from Playwright's own 1280x720 default in **both** dimensions: a
# viewport key read for width and dropped for height would pass a plant that moved only one of them.
# The control — the same page, the same readout, no `viewport` anywhere — is
# `tests/.constructs/step-observables.tflw`, under the root config.
defaults
  viewport 900 600

env local default
  api "http://localhost:4001/v1"
  web "http://localhost:8090"
